{%- comment -%}
  Prints the quick add mode a product card can really offer.

  Accepts:
  - product: product object
  - mode: the mode the card picked (none, sold_out, options, single, direct or picker)

  Quick add sends one unit per tap. A variant with a minimum or a step above 1 (volume or B2B
  pricing rules) cannot be bought that way, so the modes that swap variants hand over to the
  product page when any variant has such a rule. A single variant is kept: the card sends its own
  minimum. Prints only the mode, with no surrounding whitespace.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign resolved_mode = mode
  if mode == 'direct' or mode == 'picker'
    for rule_variant in product.variants
      if rule_variant.quantity_rule.min > 1 or rule_variant.quantity_rule.increment > 1
        assign resolved_mode = 'options'
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif
-%}
{{- resolved_mode -}}
